  "details": "avtr_9820b1cf-b73c-4e21-8546-a5b22fd1b201 \n\nThis avatar refuses to generate an imposter after attempting multiple times. It seems the issue is with the imposter settings used on the avatar, as removing them allows the imposter to generate.\n\nThe avatar has an extra left arm, one for deformations, and one assigned to the humanoid avatar description. The deforming bones have rotation constraints to move with the humanoid bones (which are able to be disabled in order to use a separate constraint system on them for differing arm motions).\n\nThese constraints however, get ignored upon imposter generation, leaving one arm T-posing. In order to combat this, I have placed 3 imposter settings components on the armature, one on the upper arm, forearm, and hand. These each have one reparent here target transform, corresponding to their respective deforming bone.\n\nAdditionally, removing all of these aside from the upper arm one still causes the same refusal to generate.",
